17170	{"artifactId":"LLD-b2e8109f42afc0dd-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-b2e8109f42afc0dd-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:26:55.515Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The widget the design specifies (8 lines until opened, 'show N more lines' / 'show less', 'new file' and binary labels, a one-line count when a step changes more than is drawn) is the widget of the approved mock docs/mocks/chat-diff-widget.html.","evidence":"docs/mocks/chat-diff-widget.html:128 `var LIMIT = 8; // diff lines shown before the widget is expanded`; :176 `more.textContent = open ? 'show less' : 'show ' + (total - LIMIT) + ' more line'...`; :123 a hunk with `kind: 'new file'`; :201 the note lists two sections of one file, a new file collapsed to 8, a binary file and the overflow line. Commit 42f0d499 says the mock follows the decision 'one widget per section of the git diff against the turn start'. [files: docs/mocks/chat-diff-widget.html]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The acceptance criteria ac1-ac7 restate the user's decisions of 2026-10-13 (c9), with nothing added and nothing left out.","evidence":"The only artifact for this story is .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b2e8109f42afc0dd-s1.json (Glob of .insrc/artifacts/*b2e8109f* returns nothing else): there is no SPEC or DEF, and the chat of 2026-10-13 is not in the repository. The design itself says the Story came with no criteria and that they are 'to be confirmed by the user when the design is approved'. Only the mock and two commit messages could be compared.","action":"At approval, have the user confirm ac1-ac7 and the stated limit (after a chat switch, panel close or reload the rest of the turn shows path lines, not widgets).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the governor diffs the whole file in process on a 'file-edit' event and the host posts 'edit-prompt'; nothing of the diff is saved; the snapshot is `git stash create` plus the text of untracked files.","evidence":"edit-governor.ts:145 `diff = deps.computeDiff(baselineContent, after, path)` and :157 `deps.render.showChat(path, diff, { review })`; defaultComputeDiff returns one hunk `{ oldStart: 1, oldLines: n, newStart: 1, newLines: m, lines }` (:236-239). chat-panel.ts:291 `showChat: (path, diff, opts) => post({ type: 'edit-prompt', ... })`, and appendEvent (:1168-1201) writes no diff row. git-baseline.ts:40 `runGit(cwd, ['stash', 'create'])`, :45 `['ls-files', '--others', '--exclude-standard']` with readText per file. Shell commands produce no 'file-edit' event (cli-adapter.ts:595 only for CLAUDE_EDIT_TOOLS = Edit, Write at :505). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/edit-governor.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/git-baseline.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The diff box is a child of a flex column that can shrink it to nothing, so `#insrc-term>*{flex-shrink:0;}` is the fix.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:649 `#insrc-term{flex:1 1 auto;min-height:0;overflow-y:auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;...}` and the design's c11 line :732 `.insrc-term-diff{...overflow:hidden;...}`. A flex item with overflow:hidden has an automatic minimum height of 0 and the default flex-shrink of 1, so it is the one child the column can squash. No flex-shrink rule exists for the transcript's children today (:650 is only `#insrc-term>div{white-space:pre-wrap;}`). Checked by reading the CSS; not rendered in a browser. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A detached, superseded or failed turn gets no onTerminal, and a followed turn has its own event path with only onEvent and onEnd.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:309 `if (detached) break;` before any sink call; :335-341 a turn that is no longer current reports nothing (`if (!isCurrent(myGen)) { if (isTerminal(ev)) { endTurn(ev, it); trySave(s); break; } continue; }`); :355-362 a throw calls reportError (sink.onError) and never onTerminal. FollowSink (:54-59) has only onEvent and onEnd, and chat-panel.ts:504-529 followLiveTurn calls appendEvent and postLive without touching the governor. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"What the design calls new does not exist yet (diff-sections.ts, the 'transcript-row' message, editPath / isError / applied, sectionsActive / abandonTurn), and what it reuses exists with the stated shape (relForGit, the adapter's memory of tool_use ids, the registry's isLong rule, renderers built through line(), pager.track).","evidence":"Grep for `transcript-row|editPath|sectionsActive|abandonTurn` over vscode-plugin/src: 0 matches; no diff-sections* file under vscode-plugin/src/chat. Reused: extension.ts:485 `const relForGit = (cwd, p) => (pathIsAbsolute(p) ? pathRelative(cwd, p) : p).split('\\\\').join('/')`; cli-adapter.ts:605 `(state.toolCommands ??= {})[block['id']] = command` and :632 the lookup by tool_use_id; render-registry.ts:331 `function isLong(s){...split('\\n').length>3||s.length>240;}`; :528, :544, :576 renderers start with `var wrap=line('')`; transcript-pager.ts:86 `function track(rowIndex,fn)`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"None. Note that the tool_use id is remembered today only when the call has a command (cli-adapter.ts:604), so remembering Edit and Write ids is new code in the edit branch at :595.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A completed codex file_change item carries a `changes` list with one entry per changed file, each with a path.","evidence":"The repository holds no sample of a real codex file_change item: `file_change` occurs only in cli-adapter.ts:728 and in a comment of edit-governor.ts, and no test fixture carries a `changes` field. The mapper today reads only `item['path']` (cli-adapter.ts:729). The design rests this on a probe run by hand (c7), which I cannot repeat here.","action":"Keep the planned live test ('live codex: a patch of two files ... yields two applied file-edit events') and add a recorded real item as a unit fixture so the shape is pinned without the live flag. Also decide whether an item whose status is failed should carry `applied`.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The points where the host must end the open diff state (before each turns.detach() and turns.stop(), in the sink's onError, at the top of the next beforeRun) cover every way a started turn stops reporting to its sink.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts has exactly one turns.stop() (:1230, cancel-turn) and five turns.detach() (:1242 new-chat, :1264 open-chat, :1493 onDidDispose, :1516 adopt, :1527 dispose); turns.invalidate() is only called right after a detach (:1243, :1265). The lifecycle's other silent exits are supersession (turn-lifecycle.ts:335) and a throw (:355-362, which calls onError only while current). One gap in timing, not in the list: Stop or a detach pressed WHILE beforeRun is still awaiting governor.beginTurn finds no diff state to end, then beforeRun creates one and the lifecycle drops the turn (:292 `if (setup.signal.aborted || !isCurrent(myGen)) return;`). That state has no held paths, so nothing is lost on screen, but its snapshot and private index file stay until the next turn's beforeRun or the next detach. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"In the build, have beforeRun check after governor.beginTurn whether the turn was stopped or detached meanwhile (for example a flag the host sets in its end-diff-state step) and abandon the governor's turn at once, so no temporary index file is left when the window closes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A 'diff' renderer built through line() is appended on the live path, on restore and on an older page, and a row that draws nothing does not upset the pager; pageBefore and latestWindow are the only two cuts.","evidence":"Older page: transcript-pager.ts:94 `reg.appendKeyed(reg.toViewModel(row),'r'+idx)`; render-registry.ts:586 `function appendKeyed(vm,key){...var n=renderRow(vm);if(n)KEYS[key]=n;return n;}` accepts a renderer that returns nothing. The pager stamps whatever was appended (`stamp(from,rowIndex)` at :68-72 loops from `from` to the children's length, so zero new nodes is fine and `last` still advances). Cuts: chat-panel.ts:321 `latestWindow(s.transcript)` and :1280 `pageBefore(session.transcript, msg.before)`; transcript-window.ts:38 latestWindow calls pageBefore. The pager already tells the registry what it trimmed (:84 `reg.forgetKeysBefore(cut);reg.forgetPendingIn(gone);`), which is where the remembered widgets can be forgotten. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/transcript-pager.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/transcript-window.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Removing 'edit-prompt', renderDiff, the seven .insrc-diff-* rules, showChat and computeDiff touches only the sites the design names and breaks no other user.","evidence":"'edit-prompt': protocol.ts:93 and :259, chat-panel.ts:291 and :927. renderDiff: chat-panel.ts:908 only. The seven rules: chat-panel.ts:733-739 (path, add, del, ctx, actions, actions button, actions button:hover). computeDiff: edit-governor.ts:54/145, chat-panel.ts:66/297, extension.ts:59/559. docs-review-panel.ts uses the class names insrc-diff-ctx (:1632, :1728) and insrc-diff-del (:1730), but it has its own renderShell and <style> (:1482, :1489) with no .insrc-diff-* rule and design-tokens.ts has none either, so it never took its look from the chat shell's rules. One consequence the design accepts without saying so: renderDiff's accept and reject buttons are the only sender of 'edit-decision' (:908), so after this change the kept message and governor.decide can no longer be reached from the chat. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"None required. Consider a one-line note in the design that 'edit-decision' and decide stay as unreachable code, or remove them in a follow-up.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The file store only appends rows and does not check a row's role, so diff rows need no store change, old sessions load unchanged, and another window's rows can land between this window's rows.","evidence":"session-file-store.ts:343-344 `const fresh = s.transcript.slice(count); if (fresh.length > 0) fs.appendText(p.rows, rowLines(fresh));`; :337-341 'A rows file longer than this store left it: another writer appended. This object's new rows still go after theirs'; rows are read with `rows.push(JSON.parse(line) as TranscriptEntry)` (:199) with no per-row check. A whole rewrite happens only when the transcript got shorter or the files are gone (:328-331), which a push-only host never causes. This confirms that linking versions by sid, not by position, is needed. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An older plugin build that opens a chat with diff rows draws each as an empty fallback line and does not fail.","evidence":"The current toViewModel has no branch for an unknown role and ends in the marker fallback: render-registry.ts:139-140 `{ kind: 'fallback', text: entry.text, collapsible: false }` (text is undefined for a diff row); the webview mirror does the same at :407. renderRow catches a throwing renderer and falls back (:389-391). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/render-registry.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A git failure is detectable without an exception: the runner never rejects, a patch over 64 MB comes back as not ok, and a failed snapshot leaves the turn without a handle.","evidence":"extension.ts:479-484 `nodeExecFile('git', ['-C', cwd, ...args], { encoding: 'utf8', maxBuffer: 64 * 1024 * 1024 }, (err, stdout) => { resolve({ ok: err === null, stdout: stdout ?? '' }); })` (exceeding maxBuffer gives a non-null err). edit-governor.ts:104-106 wraps snapshot in `safe(...)`, which logs and returns undefined, and :109 stores `handle` as undefined. The env argument is new: the runner must merge it over process.env, not replace it. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/edit-governor.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The git commands behave as the design says: `git add -A` and `git write-tree` with GIT_INDEX_FILE on a copy leave the user's index and status untouched, `git diff --relative <tree> <tree>` gives cwd-relative paths, and `git show <tree>:./<rel>` reads from a tree id.","evidence":"I have no shell in this review, so I could not run git. The design rests this on a probe by hand with git 2.53.0 (c7). The code only confirms the surrounding facts: git runs with `-C cwd` (extension.ts:481), so a relative path printed by `rev-parse --git-path index` is relative to cwd, and read already uses the `<ref>:./<rel>` form (git-baseline.ts:59).","action":"Keep the planned real-git integration test (git-baseline.integration.test.ts) as a required check of the build, and include a linked worktree and a repository with core.splitIndex in it, since both change where the index lives.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing tests the design says it replaces or keeps are where it says they are, and every one of ac1 to ac7 has at least one named test.","evidence":"protocol.test.ts:90 and :116 list 'edit-prompt' among the host kinds; extension-chat-wiring.test.ts:89 `assert.match(b, /computeDiff:\\s*defaultComputeDiff/...)`; chat-theme.test.ts:256-258 the three has() lines; chat-theme-before.json:70-76 the seven selectors; chat-panel.test.ts:967, :3538, :3548 the renderDiff assertions; edit-governor.test.ts tests at :88, :108, :121 (review tracking), :156 (editor view), :168, :179; git-baseline.test.ts has four tests (:56, :69, :83, :92). The test files named for new cases exist (session-file-store, render-registry, chat-shell, transcript-pager, transcript-window, live-cli). The acceptance table gives each of ac1-ac7 between two and nine tests. Two small gaps in the governor list: the non-git test at :134 is not mentioned, and the cross-turn test at :179 is 'kept' although it is written against showChat (:192) and must be rewritten for showSections. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/edit-governor.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/protocol.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-theme.test.ts]","action":"When building, state what happens to edit-governor.test.ts:134 and rewrite :179 against the new render seam.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":3},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-13T08:26:55.515Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
